{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1992 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "90fc0f7cc09246282618758f9f42af791c5a2f62a4ecfe989f7fc715cc71ec5d" :edb/db-before-t 1991 :edb/db-after-t 1992 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535304 50 #inst "2026-10-08T21:42:30.234Z" 13194139535304 true] [17592186068845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342889 13194139535304 true] [17592186068846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186342886 13194139535304 true] [17592186068958 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535304 true] [17592186068958 1100 "$\\int {x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186068958 1100 "What is $\\intx^{2}(\\ln x)^{2}dx$?" 13194139535304 false] [17592186068958 1145 "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{9}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{27}-\\frac{2D}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{27}(9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{3}.$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186302503 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342885 13194139535304 true] [17592186342885 1034 "\\pi^2+6" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342885 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342885 1111 #uuid "abf314cb-4a76-593a-9762-f3e7e2f80384" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342887 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1089 "q-352122" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{e}81{x}^{2}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(${{field-1}}$)$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1113 #uuid "2c983f78-21f8-572b-a438-e637d8900e35" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342886 1145 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=81{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 81{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=27{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 81{x}^{2}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}(27{x}^{3})-\\int (27{x}^{3})(\\frac{2{log}_{4}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =27{x}^{3}{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{54}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{4}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{4}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{4}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{4}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{4}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 81{x}^{2}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =27{x}^{3}{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{54}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{4}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+D) \\\\  & =27{x}^{3}{({log}_{4}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{18{x}^{3}{log}_{4}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}+\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{27{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{18{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+\\frac{6{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(27{ln}^{2}⁡x-18\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+6)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{54D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation, we used the change of base formula ${log}_{4}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}81{x}^{2}({log}_{4}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(27{ln}^{2}⁡x-18\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+6)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(27{ln}^{2}⁡e-18\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+6)-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(27{ln}^{2}⁡1-18\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(27-18+6)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(0-0+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{15{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}-\\frac{6}{{ln}^{2}⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡4}(\\,15{e}^{3}-6\\,)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342888 13194139535304 true] [17592186342887 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535304 true] [17592186342887 1041 "field-1" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342887 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342888 13194139535304 true] [17592186342887 1110 #uuid "48aa3d5f-c385-5f5a-8c2c-91acce4a95fd" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342888 1034 "15e^3-6" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342888 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342888 1111 #uuid "a9dc516f-68c4-522a-9ee8-2895a63acc72" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1017 #edb/ref 17592186342890 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1089 "q-50224" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1100 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1113 #uuid "56fb8dc5-e5bf-5cf9-a079-52d59d17ab55" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342889 1145 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+1)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }5{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(5{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-(5{\\pi }^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +10\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -(-(5(0)^{2}+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡0))-10\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0-10\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}+1-10+1-10 \\\\  & =5{\\pi }^{2}-18\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342891 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342892 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342893 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342894 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1000 #edb/ref 17592186342895 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1041 "selection" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1104 #edb/ref 17592186342891 13194139535304 true] [17592186342890 1110 #uuid "7b9ec316-9004-587b-92b8-2f8bbacd3830" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342891 1034 "5{\\pi }^{2}-18" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342891 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342891 1111 #uuid "2b6cfa1b-c310-5444-bb68-2613298dd93d" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342892 1034 "5\\pi +18" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342892 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342892 1111 #uuid "629b7496-b810-5ce2-872c-9ab4b9e19e3b" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342893 1034 "5{\\pi }^{2}" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342893 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342893 1111 #uuid "2b5c6185-868a-55be-86d2-ce4300e610b9" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342894 1034 "5\\pi +9" 13194139535304 true] [17592186342894 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535304 true] [17592186342894 1111 #uuid